Description: Add output mirroring
 Regolith's X11 session can mirror two monitors, for example a laptop
 panel and a projector, but sway has no mirroring: `output <name> mirror`
 is rejected, and placing two outputs at the same position keeps them
 two separate monitors, with their own workspaces, bars and backgrounds.
 .
 Add `output <name> mirror <source>|off`. A mirror shows the area of the
 layout that its source covers, cursor included, scaled by the same
 factor on both axes to fit its own mode and transform, centred, with
 black bars around it. Output scales don't change the picture. While it
 mirrors, the output takes no space in the layout, has no workspaces
 (they move to other outputs as when it is disabled) and no wl_output,
 so clients, bars and backgrounds only see the source. Its mode,
 transform and color profile still apply.
 .
 Mirroring takes effect while both outputs are connected and enabled;
 otherwise the output works as a normal one and switches as the source
 connects, disconnects, is enabled or disabled. While the source is
 powered off, the mirror is black. Self-mirroring and chains are
 rejected. get_outputs gains a "mirror" key and lists a mirror as active
 with the rect of its source; output management clients see a mirror
 at the position of its source.
